 * physically back. scheduleNode() asks this module, per candidate node:
 * "sum of guaranteed RAM of every running VM (customer AND platform VMs,
 * read from the real configs) + this new VM" vs physical RAM minus the host
 * reserve, and "real used + this new VM" vs physical RAM. See
 * ramGuardVerdict() for the exact rule and the env knobs.
 *
 * Reads: GET /nodes/<n>/status, GET /nodes/<n>/qemu, and
 * GET /nodes/<n>/qemu/<vmid>/config?current=1 per running VM. Cached per node
 * for SNAPSHOT_TTL_MS; each read is time-boxed so an unresponsive node
 * cannot stall checkout. A node whose snapshot cannot be read is reported as
